<A NAME=S9></A>
<H2>Summary</H2>
<UL>
<LI>Plan a big application the same way as a small one: what it remembers, what happens.<P>
<LI>The <CODE>Binder</CODE> module draws the binder and says what is at a point; the program decides what
a click means.<P>
<LI>A base class can describe an <I>interface</I>: every method the window may call, each doing nothing, so
subclasses write only what they need.<P>
<LI>Sections record where they drew their entries (<CODE>box</CODE>), and <CODE>at</CODE> finds the entry
at a point; <CODE>findLast</CODE> searches from the end.<P>
<LI>Classes are values: a function can return a class expression, and a list of classes can be turned into
objects with <CODE>map</CODE>.<P>
<LI><CODE>...array</CODE> in a call spreads an array into separate arguments.<P>
<LI>A model written without windows can be reused unchanged by another program: the organiser's Address
section is !Contacts' <CODE>Book</CODE> and <CODE>editCard</CODE>.<P>
<LI>One file can hold several collections; a generic <CODE>Collection</CODE> class serves them all.<P>
</UL>

